Feature: ignore
  The ignore file lists patterns of targets that the source state does not manage. Patterns
  match target paths; a pattern starting with ! stops a target being ignored.

  # Background: the txtar script's home2. The first three scenarios use its home, which needs
  # apply, ignored and templates, so they stay skeletons.
  Background:
    Given an empty home directory
    And the source state manages:
      | target                | kind      | contents                          |
      | ~/.dir                | directory |                                   |
      | ~/.dir/file.txt       | file      | # contents of .dir/file.txt       |
      | ~/.dir/subdir         | directory |                                   |
      | ~/.dir/subdir/file.txt | file     | # contents of .dir/subdir/file.txt |
      | ~/.file.txt           | file      | # contents of .file.txt           |

